C o m p i l a t i o n


   1  *Trying out simplest model for project
   2  *current set: regions
   3  *will have to complicate regions sets to add more countries
   4  *will have to add time dimension, will also be a new set
   5  *NEW SET SHOULD BE ALUMINUM PRIMARY OR SECONDARY: set al /primary, secondary/;
   6   
   7  set r /USA, ROW/;
   8   
   9  *parameters = essentially cost curves, FIND BETTER NUMBERS - currently using rough estimated numbers from AI
  10  *prices USD/metric ton , qty = metric tons , currently total aluminum (primary + secondary)
  11  parameter
  12  *price of aluminum USA and ROW
  13  pbar(r) /USA 2855, ROW 2420/,
  14  *qty supplied aluminum USA and ROW
  15  qbar_s(r) /USA 2236000, ROW 96000000/,
  16  *qty demanded aluminum USA and ROW
  17  qbar_d(r) /USA 5830000, ROW 92406000/,
  18  *elasticity of supply generally -- this will have to break out for primary secondary, different for each country
  19  e_s /0.4/,
  20  *elasticity of demand generally -- ^^
  21  e_d /-0.4/;
  22   
  23  *currently based off of Pd = a + b*Qd, Ps = c + d*Qs, where a,b,c,d are parameters
  24  *will have to break out for primary and secondary aluminun and include the different elasticities for each country
  25  parameter a(r),b(r),c(r),d(r);
  26   
  27  b(r) = pbar(r) / (e_d * qbar_d(r));
  28  a(r) = pbar(r) - b(r) * qbar_d(r);
  29  d(r) = pbar(r) / (e_s * qbar_s(r));
  30  c(r) = pbar(r) - d(r) * qbar_s(r);
  31   
  32  *t will essentially be the cost of transportation/logistics?
  33  scalar t ;
  34  t = pbar('ROW') - pbar('USA');
  35   
  36  *varibales - will have to have more specefic to primary and secondary
  37  positive variable Qd(r), Qs(r);
  38  positive variable X "exports";
  39  variable W "total welfare";
  40   
  41  *will have to have market clearing for different countries and primary/secondary once added
  42  *also will have to add different constrains ie EU restiricitions on secondary exports once 2027....
  43  equation objfn, market_clearing_USA, market_clearing_ROW;
  44   
  45  objfn.. W =e=
  46     sum(r, a(r) * Qd(r) + b(r) * Qd(r) *Qd(r) /2 - c(r) * Qs(r) - d(r) *Qs(r) * Qs(r) / 2 ) - t * X;
  47   
  48  market_clearing_USA.. Qd('USA') + X =e= Qs('USA');
  49  market_clearing_ROW.. Qd('ROW') =e= Qs('ROW') + X;
  50   
  51  model simple /all/;
  52   
  53  solve simple using QCP maximizing W;
  54  parameter rep(*,*,r);
  55  rep ("BAU", "Qd",r) = Qd.l(r);
  56  rep("BAU", "Qs",r) = Qs.l(r);
  57  rep("BAU", "P", "USA") = market_clearing_USA.m;
  58  rep("BAU", "P", "ROW") = market_clearing_ROW.m;
  59   
  60  execute_unload "simple.gdx" ;
  61   
  62   
  63  *conversion to MCP


